> One of the things I've been noticing lately is that I accumulate
> combat wands and rarely use them.  Now part of this may be that my
> most successful characters have been, as expected for my experience,
> Barbarians, Valkyries and Samurai.  For these, it is, "If I can beat
> it up, why waste a charge on my wand?"  Even with these, though, I've
> died several times in melee with several wands unused in my
> inventory.  I typically only zap them when I get several enemies to
> line up.
>
> How do you all decide when to zap and when not to?

I prefer to zap when a monster is still out of dagger range or when
I'm running low on daggers.  Also I zap at monsters powerful
relative to my current level - The first time I see a mumak I start
zapping with the meanest wand I have immediately.

I prefer to save my wands when dealing with popcorn monsters,
whatever that means given my current level.

I will save death wands for Rodney.  I will save cold wands for the
Medusa level, the castles and the deeper swamps.

I will burn most other combat wands within a 3-4 levels of finding
them.  I figure if I have more than 3 combat wands I definitely
need to start using them, and if I have less than 3 combat wands
I need to use daggers more.

The one combat wand I under use is teleport away.  Only the
very strongest monsters know how to teleport so I should use
them on everything from minotaurs on down.



